From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 00:27:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] avdevice/v4l2: do not re-queue a buffer released after close

The framework frees the packets it buffered for a demuxer after the
demuxer's read_close, so a packet whose buffer is a mapped capture
buffer can be released once the device is gone. The release callback
then queued the buffer on the closed file descriptor, and every such
packet logged "ioctl(VIDIOC_QBUF): Bad file descriptor".

Mark the descriptor closed in read_close and skip the re-queue for a
buffer released after it. There is no capture left for the buffer to
serve.

Signed-off-by: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 libavdevice/v4l2.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libavdevice/v4l2.c b/libavdevice/v4l2.c
index c38ecbb..a51fc70 100644
--- a/libavdevice/v4l2.c
+++ b/libavdevice/v4l2.c
@@ -466,6 +466,11 @@ static void mmap_release_buffer(void *opaque, uint8_t *data)
     buf.length   = s->multiplanar ? VIDEO_MAX_PLANES : 0;
     av_free(buf_descriptor);
 
+    /* A packet can outlive the device: the framework frees the packets it
+     * buffered after read_close. Such a buffer has no queue to return to. */
+    if (s->fd < 0)
+        return;
+
     enqueue_buffer(s, &buf);
 }
 
@@ -1052,6 +1057,7 @@ static int v4l2_read_close(AVFormatContext *ctx)
 
     ff_timefilter_destroy(s->timefilter);
     v4l2_close(s->fd);
+    s->fd = -1;
     return 0;
 }
 
